      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i'll try the stretch. but do you think i should maybe try a bit more than just the knee-to-chest thing? like, i saw a video online where people do these really deep spinal twists and even lie on a hard roller to really force the back to pop. since it feels like something is \"stuck\" or pinching, wouldn't a more intense stretch or a forceful crack actually be more effective at releasing that nerve pressure? i'm kinda scared it's more than a strain because of the numbness in my foot, but i'd rather just fix it myself at home.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
